 ## [Unreleased]
 
+## [18.14.0-fork.1] - 2026-10-30
+
+### Removed
+
+- Removed the fork's auth-gateway access control (managed users and tokens, ACLs, credential pools, the management and audit APIs, `/v1/models` `reasoning`/`thinking_efforts` fields), `acquireAuthCredential`, `AuthStorage.listStoredCredentialsByIds` and `upsertCredentialAsync`, `oauth.accessAt`, `health.check({ credentialIds })`, and the SQLite store's re-login row reactivation. The auth gateway and broker store are upstream's.
+
+### Changed
+
+- Re-based onto upstream v18.14.0. `AuthStorage.resolveApiKeySelection` and credential selection policies stay, and an OAuth row they resolve now carries its access token, so upstream's 401 recovery adopts a peer's refreshed token instead of spending the refresh token again.
+
+## [18.12.2-fork.1] - 2026-10-19
+
+### Changed
+
+- Auth-gateway scoped client tokens authenticate after the gateway and managed tokens as a `client` principal that is never an admin; the fork's chat routes resolve, refresh and rotate a client's credentials only inside the accounts it is bound to. `createAuthGatewayRouter().route()` takes the admitted principal before the scoped client.
+
+## [18.9.2-fork.1] - 2026-10-12
+
+### Added
+
+- `AuthGatewayRouteOptions.resolveVariantBase` names the catalog model a resolved routing variant was cloned from; model ACL deny rules on that model also deny the variant.
+
+### Changed
+
+- The fork's default account, account priority and selection policies now run inside upstream's account-pool session restrictions: a restricted session never selects, rotates to, or announces a default-account fallover to an account outside its pool.
+
+## [18.6.1-fork.2] - 2026-10-09
+
+### Added
+
+- Этап aigw2 3A: прокси на запрос (`webSocketProxy`, `fetchImpl` для refresh, `ctrl.fetch` для device login), восстановление PKCE-входа через `pkceVerifier`/`resume()`.
+- `postmortem.releaseSigtermHandler()` передаёт SIGTERM встраивающему серверу, сохраняя все сторонние обработчики; cleanup при exit остаётся.
+
+### Fixed
+
+- Явные типы `UsageCache`/`UsageService` снимают циклический вывод типов при сборке деклараций TypeScript.
+
+## [18.5.1-fork.1] - 2026-10-03
+
+### Changed
+
+- The fork's auth-gateway management API, ACLs, account pools, and audit log now run inside upstream's `createAuthGatewayRouter`, behind upstream's HTTP transport: gateway bearer tokens sent anywhere but `Authorization` are rejected with `400`, and `trustProxyHeaders` controls whether forwarded client addresses are honored.
+
+## [18.3.0-fork.1] - 2026-09-24
+
+### Added
+
+- Auth gateway `GET /v1/models` rows now advertise `reasoning` and `thinking_efforts` (the served model's effort ladder) so clients can offer the levels the gateway actually honors.
+
+### Fixed
+
+- Fixed Claude Opus 5.5 failing the first tool-forcing request with `400 tool_choice: type "tool" and "any" are not supported for this model`; forced tool choice is now downgraded to `auto` for Opus 5.5 on every host, which also keeps thinking at the requested effort.
+
+## [18.2.9-fork.1] - 2026-09-23
+
+### Added
+
+- Gateway routes for every non-chat modality now resolve credentials through the caller's account pool: `resolveGatewayApiKey` and `buildGatewayApiKeyResolver` take the request's boot options and honour the `credentialScope` the router installs, so an ACL denial, an empty pool, and pool-scoped rotation behave the same on `/v1/embeddings` as on `/v1/chat/completions`.
+- ACL rules accept the new `systemone`, `images`, `speech`, `transcriptions`, `embeddings`, `rerank`, and `video` route families.
+
